## 10. Version Control Hygiene

```bash
# ✅ Commit convention
feat(auth): add password reset flow
fix(api): resolve race condition in payment processing
refactor(db): extract query builder to shared utility
test(e2e): add checkout flow coverage
docs(api): update OpenAPI spec for v2 endpoints

# Rules:
# - Subject: max 72 chars, imperative mood ("add", not "added")
# - Body: explain WHY, not WHAT (the diff shows WHAT)
# - One logical change per commit
# - Small, focused commits > large, sweeping commits
```

## Clean Code Checklist

- [ ] No magic numbers — all values are named constants
- [ ] All names are descriptive and intention-revealing
- [ ] Functions are under 30 lines with a single responsibility
- [ ] No deeply nested conditionals — guard clauses and early returns used
- [ ] No copy-pasted logic — duplicated code extracted to shared utilities
- [ ] Comments explain WHY, not WHAT
- [ ] Business logic is encapsulated, not scattered across UI components
- [ ] Every `catch` block handles or re-throws — no empty catches
